From: pocket_vm developers <pocket-vm@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] um: arm userspace stubs with parent-death signal before exec

The embedded stub asks for PR_SET_PDEATHSIG only after exec. If the UML
creator dies between clone and the first instruction of the new executable,
the stub can be reparented before it arms the signal and survive the kernel.

Arm SIGKILL in the clone trampoline before execveat and immediately recheck
the expected parent. PR_SET_PDEATHSIG is retained across this non-privileged
exec, while the existing in-stub call remains a defensive second arm.

This is a lifecycle/correctness invariant for the no-cgroup runtime. It does
not claim to make cooperative UML safe for hostile guest userspace.
---
 arch/um/os-Linux/skas/process.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/um/os-Linux/skas/process.c b/arch/um/os-Linux/skas/process.c
index d6c22f8aa06d..aced69dc4aab 100644
--- a/arch/um/os-Linux/skas/process.c
+++ b/arch/um/os-Linux/skas/process.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <sys/wait.h>
 #include <sys/stat.h>
 #include <sys/socket.h>
+#include <sys/prctl.h>
 #include <asm/unistd.h>
 #include <as-layout.h>
 #include <init.h>
@@ -283,6 +284,7 @@ struct tramp_data {
 	struct stub_data *stub_data;
 	/* 0 is inherited, 1 is the kernel side */
 	int sockpair[2];
+	pid_t expected_parent;
 };
 
 #ifndef CLOSE_RANGE_CLOEXEC
@@ -300,6 +302,18 @@ static int userspace_tramp(void *data)
 	};
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Arm this before exec so there is no window in which a stub can be
+	 * reparented and then survive the UML kernel. PR_SET_PDEATHSIG follows
+	 * the creating thread, which is the lifetime relationship we need.
+	 */
+	if (prctl(PR_SET_PDEATHSIG, SIGKILL) < 0)
+		exit(6);
+
+	/* The parent may have died immediately before prctl(). */
+	if (getppid() != tramp_data->expected_parent)
+		exit(7);
+
 	if (using_seccomp) {
 		init_data.signal_handler = STUB_CODE +
 					   (unsigned long) stub_signal_interrupt -
@@ -449,5 +463,6 @@ int start_userspace(struct mm_id *mm_id)
 	struct tramp_data tramp_data = {
 		.stub_data = proc_data,
+		.expected_parent = getpid(),
 	};
 	void *stack;
 	unsigned long sp;
-- 
